{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"submission_c21.json\",\"summary\":\"Fixed direct check (action=check) for unit-claim-install-snapshot-alignment, preflight-validated with valid=True and no diagnostics.\\n\\nDesign: plan_c4.json plus harness_snap_test.go seed a log with a configuration entry at index 1 and command entries through index 5, build a node with background goroutines disabled (conf.skipStartup, TrailingLogs 0) whose only configured voter is another server, install a snapshot at index 3 through the production handler installSnapshot, and report both the declared state and the result. Declarative prerequisite: holds_entries_above_installed_index true. Monitor applicability: rejected false (the install was accepted). Property: the receiver's effective last entry must not exceed the installed snapshot index, expressed as within_installed_snapshot true with identity op_id, evaluated from emitted event fields rather than tests_passed.\\n\\nConstruction evidence (not the formal observation): the harness runs locally in a copy of the captured module and shows the state the obligation is about — compaction reported 'from=1 to=3', two entries survived, lastApplied and snapshot index became 3, the effective last entry stayed (5, term 1), and within_installed_snapshot was false.\\n\\nDeclared adaptations, kept explicit rather than hidden: the handler is invoked directly because skipStartup leaves no main loop (production dispatches the same function from the transport consumer channel); an explicit substitute goroutine answers restore futures with success because runFSM is absent, and the substitute never touches log or snapshot state; the log content is written to the caller-owned LogStore and the snapshot payload is synthetic because the harness FSM ignores snapshot content; TrailingLogs is set to 0 so compaction is not skipped by the trailing-log guard. No target code is modified.\\n\\nRetained uncertainties: whether a real leader drives a follower into this state, how long the tail persists before the next AppendEntries truncates it, and whether any vote or election can depend on the window. The plan also carries the documented-transient alternative for the legality of the missing alignment step. No verdict is claimed; fresh execution of these fixed bytes and a checker-correspondence review still remain.\"}"}}
